                <pb facs="0515" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg465"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 248.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I cabled you the news of the shooting of a
                    Mr. Wilson, an American, by the Nicaraguan military governor at Bluefields. I
                    had received no particulars. I called upon the authorities here for an
                    explanation, and I inclose the response of the Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker.</hi></signed></closer>





